<task id="020" project="messaging-communication-app-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Regarding-mode extension to the `CommunicationTimeline` component (`@spaarke/ui-components`): threads-as-collapsible-groups → per-thread interleaved email+chat timelines, backed by the new `by-regarding` endpoint</title>
    <phase>W2 — Record Threads View (Surface 1)</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>12</estimated-hours>
    <deps>010</deps>
    <blocks>021</blocks>
    <tags>frontend, fluent-ui, communication</tags>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Extends the load-bearing shared-library `CommunicationTimeline` React component (`.tsx`/`.ts` in `@spaarke/ui-components`) with a NEW render mode that becomes the R2 record-level message surface; architecture-level decisions (regarding read model, collapsible-group state, group→thread timeline reuse, access-parity trust boundary); blocks the PCF packaging (021). ADR-021 (Fluent v9), ADR-012 (shared lib), ADR-028 (auth decoupling), NFR-03 (server-filtered, no client access logic) bind. FULL is non-negotiable.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W2</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>All-client TypeScript in `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CommunicationTimeline/**` — disjoint by file + language from the concurrent BFF (C#) and schema tracks. Within W2 this is the serial root (021 packages it, 022 places it), but it runs safely alongside other waves. 023 (VisualHost config) touches no shared files.</parallel-reason>
    <fr-refs>FR-03</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Extend the shipped `CommunicationTimeline` component (R1 task 060) in `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CommunicationTimeline/` with a **regarding mode**. Today the component renders a single thread (thread-id mode). Add a mode that takes a regarding record `(entityType, id)` and renders **all of that record's threads as collapsible groups** — each group header shows the thread name + message count; expanding a group reveals that thread's **interleaved email+chat message timeline** (the exact R1 rendering).

    The regarding mode MUST (FR-03):
    - **Take `(entityType, id)`** as input (a new prop shape / discriminated mode) instead of a single `threadId`.
    - **Call the new `by-regarding` endpoint** (task 010): `GET /api/communications/by-regarding/{entityType}/{id}`, via the injected `authenticatedFetch` — returns all threads + messages for the record in the same DTO shape as R1 reads.
    - **Render threads as collapsible groups** — the collapsed group shows the thread `sprk_name` + a message count; expanding renders the per-thread interleaved timeline. Default collapse/expand behavior is a design decision (state it in notes).
    - **Interleave email + chat by timestamp** within each expanded thread — REUSE the R1 `buildTimeline`/`MessageRow`/`ChannelBadge` rendering; do NOT fork or re-implement the row/interleave/nesting engine.
    - **NO client-side access logic** — the component renders whatever the server returns. The `by-regarding` endpoint already applies R1's impersonation + 2-rule (privacy + internal-only) filter (NFR-03). The component MUST NOT re-derive privacy, hide rows, or filter by access client-side.

    All network I/O flows through the injected `authenticatedFetch` prop + the existing `communicationTimelineApi` service — add a `readByRegarding(entityType, id, {authenticatedFetch, ...})` wrapper. The component MUST NOT import `@spaarke/auth` (ADR-028 / shared-lib decoupling). Fluent UI v9 only (ADR-021): `@fluentui/react-components` + `makeStyles` + `tokens`; dark mode passes through the host `FluentProvider`; no hardcoded colors. There is NO client-side ACS SDK anywhere (R1 NFR-04 carries into R2) — the timeline reads persisted `sprk_communication` records via the BFF only.

    Do NOT build the PCF wrapper here (task 021) or place it on forms (022) — this task extends the shared render engine only.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior React 18 + TypeScript developer fluent in Fluent UI v9 (`makeStyles`/`tokens`/`FluentProvider`) and the shipped `CommunicationTimeline` engine (`buildTimeline`, `MessageRow`, `ChannelBadge`, `useThreadPoll`, the reducer) + the `authenticatedFetch`-injection idiom (ADR-028 decoupling). Comfortable extending a component with a second render mode without regressing the existing thread-id mode.
  </role>

  <goal>
    The `CommunicationTimeline` component in `@spaarke/ui-components` supports a **regarding mode** that takes `(entityType, id)`, calls the `by-regarding` endpoint (task 010) via the injected `authenticatedFetch`, and renders the record's threads as collapsible groups (name + message count) each expanding to the R1 interleaved email+chat timeline. The existing thread-id mode is unchanged. No client-side access logic (server-filtered). No `@spaarke/auth` import and no `@azure/communication-*` import (grep-verified). `npm run build` + `npm run lint` clean; dark-mode + semantic-token compliant (ADR-021).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Surface 1 of R2 is the record-level regarding-mode Timeline placed on all 11 regarding-family entity forms. R1 shipped the per-thread polling Timeline; R2 adds the "all threads for THIS record, grouped" view on top of it (spec §Scope Surface 1, FR-03). The read model is the new `by-regarding` endpoint (task 010) which extends `CommunicationThreadReadService` + `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery` + `ICommunicationAccessFilter` — the blessed R1 impersonation read path — and is entity-set-agnostic across all 11 families.

      §11 Component Justification — this is **extend-only, no new component**. The spec explicitly lists regarding-mode Timeline (FR-03/04) as "Extend-only (no §11 justification needed): extends `CommunicationTimeline`". Existing: the R1 `CommunicationTimeline` renders a single thread. Extension: add a regarding mode that groups threads and reuses the same row/interleave engine — do NOT create a second timeline component or fork the render path. Cost-of-doing-nothing: without this mode FR-03 has no render surface and the `by-regarding` endpoint (010) has no consumer. The failure mode is a named contract failure (FR-03), not "future flexibility".

      Access parity (NFR-03) is a hard trust-boundary rule: the `by-regarding` endpoint applies R1's impersonation + 2-rule (privacy + internal-only) filter server-side. The component renders what the BFF returns and MUST NOT re-derive privacy or filter rows client-side — mirroring the R1 timeline's "renders what the BFF returns" contract (`docs/standards/DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md`).

      ADR-026 Path-A exception (spec §ADR Tensions / R1 precedent): R2's UI surface is the OOB main form + PCFs, not a Code Page — this component is the render engine that task 021 packages as a form-bound PCF. Cite the Path-A exception in the PR touching this UI surface.
    </background>
