  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read the shipped `CommunicationTimeline.tsx`, `.types.ts`, `.reducer.ts`, `.buildTimeline.ts`, the subcomponents, and `communicationTimelineApi.ts` to lock the existing thread-id mode contract and the reusable render engine. Read spec FR-03/FR-01, NFR-03/NFR-04, and the task-010 `by-regarding` DTO shape (same DTO as R1 reads) to fix the read model.</step>
    <step order="2">Read ADR-021 + `fluent-v9-component/SKILL.md` for Fluent v9 conventions and `DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md` to confirm the server-filtered / no-client-access-logic boundary (NFR-03).</step>
    <step order="3">Extend `CommunicationTimeline.types.ts`: add a discriminated mode (e.g. `mode: 'thread'` with `threadId` vs `mode: 'regarding'` with `entityType` + `id`), a `RegardingThreadGroup { threadId; name; messageCount; messages: TimelineMessage[] }` shape, and the collapse/expand state additions. Keep all existing thread-id-mode types intact.</step>
    <step order="4">Extend `communicationTimelineApi.ts`: add `readByRegarding(entityType, id, {authenticatedFetch, bffBaseUrl})` — a thin typed wrapper over the injected `authenticatedFetch` calling `GET /api/communications/by-regarding/{entityType}/{id}`; mirror the existing wrappers' typed-error contract. NO ACS imports, NO `@spaarke/auth`.</step>
    <step order="5">Extend `CommunicationTimeline.reducer.ts`: add group/expand state (which thread groups are expanded) and a `SET_REGARDING_GROUPS` action; keep the existing thread-id-mode actions untouched.</step>
    <step order="6">Author `subcomponents/ThreadGroup.tsx`: a collapsible group header (thread `sprk_name` + message count, expand/collapse chevron, semantic tokens, `aria-expanded`) that, when expanded, renders the per-thread interleaved timeline by REUSING `buildTimeline` + `MessageRow` + `ChannelBadge`.</step>
    <step order="7">Extend `CommunicationTimeline.tsx`: branch on mode. In regarding mode, call `readByRegarding`, group the returned threads, render a list of `ThreadGroup`s; in thread-id mode, keep the R1 behavior unchanged. Add `role="region"`/`aria-label` landmarks for the grouped view. Do NOT add any client-side access/privacy filtering — render exactly what the endpoint returns (NFR-03).</step>
    <step order="8">Update `CommunicationTimeline/index.ts` to export the new regarding-mode types; confirm the shared-lib barrel (`src/components/index.ts` line ~221) still re-exports the component (add new type exports there only if they are not already carried by the wildcard).</step>
    <step order="9">Run `npm run build` + `npm run lint` in `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/` (use `npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund` if a fresh install is needed; NOT `npm ci`). Both MUST be clean. Grep-verify NO `@azure/communication` import and NO `@spaarke/auth` import under `CommunicationTimeline/**` + `communicationTimelineApi.ts`. Confirm the existing thread-id-mode tests still pass.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the changed files (focus: thread-id mode not regressed, no client-side access logic (NFR-03), reuse-not-fork of the render engine, no `@spaarke/auth`/ACS import, Fluent v9 semantic tokens); `adr-check` against ADR-021/ADR-028/ADR-012/ADR-026 + `spec.md` (FR-03, NFR-03, NFR-04). Address Critical + High findings.</step>
    <step order="10">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (020 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (mode-discrimination shape, default group collapse/expand behavior, group ordering, the `readByRegarding` DTO mapping, how the R1 render engine was reused).</step>
  </steps>

